{
  "name": "swim_up",
  "//": "SWIMMING UP (Space held under water): upright, chin up. A vertical breaststroke -- the arms reach overhead, pull down and out to the sides, the hands come back up the chest and shoot overhead again -- over a frog kick that tucks the knees as the hands recover and drives out as they reach. Only played below the surface: at the surface the same input is treading (pose.cpp). Rotations: hips = lean Z (+ = right) of pitch X (+ = forward) of roll Y; every other part = sweep Y of flex X of abduction Z. A hanging limb: X negative = forward/up, positive = back; Z negative = the RIGHT limb out from the side. Knees +X bend, elbows -X bend. Hips pos in decimetres. All six swim clips share one 1200 ms period and one playhead (pose.cpp, the swim family), so a blend of two directions strokes in step.",
  "sidecarVoxelsPerMetre": 10,
  "durationMs": 1200,
  "loop": true,
  "mode": "override",
